icial_organization","credibility":0.99}],"evidence":[],"assessment":{"confidence":0.96},"verification":{"status":"verified"},"data":{"question":"What new mechanisms emerge when Depth 2 people, vendors, contracts and source documents are expanded?","method":"Breadth-first expansion of every substantive person, organization, contract and primary document discovered at Depth 2.","framework":"institutional network, procurement continuity, policy diffusion and downstream reuse","input_ids":["starintel:relation:corrine-burger-interim-ceo-columbus-partnership","starintel:relation:corrine-burger-former-jpmorganchase","starintel:relation:corrine-burger-cochairs-smart-columbus","starintel:relation:jordan-davis-chief-of-staff-andhealth","starintel:relation:jordan-davis-remains-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:matt-scantland-leads-andhealth","starintel:relation:matt-scantland-columbus-partnership","starintel:relation:michael-stevens-led-smart-columbus","starintel:relation:elon-simms-cochairs-smart-columbus","starintel:relation:kenneth-wilson-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:william-murdock-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:nancy-kramer-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:nancy-kramer-ibm","starintel:relation:matt-habash-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:calvin-cooper-smart-columbus-board","starintel:relation:electrification-coalition-advised-smart-columbus","starintel:relation:electrification-coalition-advised-paul-allen-foundation","starintel:relation:gpd-managed-smart-columbus-charging","starintel:relation:gpd-supports-greenlane","starintel:relation:smart-columbus-coauthored-green-it-playbook-rackspace","starintel:event:smart-columbus-board-roster-conflict-2026","starintel:event:columbus-partnership-leadership-transition-2026","starintel:event:accenture-acquired-pillar-technology-2018","starintel:contract:columbus-pillar-accenture-smart-city-it","starintel:contract:columbus-hntb-smart-city-program-management","starintel:contract:columbus-hntb-smart-lighting-phase-4-2026","starintel:relation:columbus-partnership-electrification-coalition-contract","starintel:relation:columbus-partnership-navigant-contract","starintel:relation:columbus-partnership-civitasnow-contract","starintel:relation:columbus-partnership-fahlgren-mortine-contract","starintel:event:electrification-coalition-accelerate-your-city-2020","starintel:event:andhealth-financing-2021","starintel:event:andhealth-columbus-expansion-2025","starintel:event:greenlane-joint-venture-2022-2023","starintel:grant:south-coast-aqmd-greenlane-2024","starintel:event:smart-columbus-green-it-playbook-2","starintel:event:connectus-digital-equity-commitment"],"findings":["Smart Columbus governance combines City, County, regional planning, nonprofit and corporate representatives; official board pages are not synchronized.","Personnel movement preserves network continuity: Jordan Davis moved to AndHealth while remaining on the Smart Columbus board, and AndHealth leadership remains connected to the Columbus Partnership.","Pillar/Accenture and HNTB occupied core implementation and program-management roles through repeated contract modifications.","Navigant, CivitasNow, Fahlgren Mortine and the Electrification Coalition supplied measurement, adoption, communications and policy-advisory functions.","The Electrification Coalition and Smart Columbus converted local implementation lessons into national replication materials.","GPD's later Greenlane work is a downstream expertise-and-capital branch, not evidence that Greenlane investors controlled Columbus decisions.","Current programs such as Green IT, ConnectUS and LinkUS extend the public-private implementation model beyond the original Smart City grant."],"conclusions":["The strongest supported mechanism is a long-lived implementation-to-replication network rather than direct WEF command.","WEF-linked corporations overlap with governance and vendor layers, but association does not establish coordinated control.","The next depth should reconstruct decision records, deliverables, full contract ledgers and specific framework-to-policy traces."],"limitations":["Authorized ceilings are not final outlays.","Some current web pages are stale or internally inconsistent.","No direct WEF payment, binding mandate, fraud or bribery was identified."],"unresolved":["Exact Smart Columbus board appointment and departure dates.","Complete HNTB and Accenture contract modification ledgers and deliverables.","Whether WEF roadmaps or toolkits appear in local work products.","Ownership and reuse rights for Smart Columbus operating-system and playbook assets.","Current governance and procurement records for LinkUS, Green IT and ConnectUS."],"confidence":0.96}}
